  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Deal 12 cards each and 6 to talon. Auction to determine declarer and contract. In king-calling contracts declarer names a suit; holder of that king is partner (hidden until king is played). Declarer may exchange with talon in some contracts. Announcements (bonuses, kontra) then play. Follow suit; must trump if unable. Highest trump or highest of led suit wins trick. Count card points; declarer's side needs 36+ in positive contracts.",
    Player: "Deal 12 cards each and 6 to talon. Auction to determine declarer and contract. In king-calling contracts declarer names a suit; holder of that king is partner (hidden until king is played). Declarer may exchange with talon in some contracts. Announcements (bonuses, kontra) then play. Follow suit; must trump if unable. Highest trump or highest of led suit wins trick. Count card points; declarer's side needs 36+ in positive contracts.",
    objective: "In positive contracts, the declarer's side must take at least 36 of the 70 available card points. Negative contracts have objectives like losing all tricks or winning an exact number of tricks.",
    gameplay: "Deal 12 cards each and 6 to talon. Auction to determine declarer and contract. In king-calling contracts declarer names a suit; holder of that king is partner (hidden until king is played). Declarer may exchange with talon in some contracts. Announcements (bonuses, kontra) then play. Follow suit; must trump if unable. Highest trump or highest of led suit wins trick. Count card points; declarer's side needs 36+ in positive contracts.",
    keyRules: [
      "Deal 12 cards each, 6 to talon; deal in two packets of 6 anticlockwise from dealer's right.",
      'Auction to determine declarer; forehand may say Mein Spiel; three consecutive passes end bidding.',
      "In Rufer/Solo/Besserrufer declarer calls a king of a suit; that king's holder is partner (hidden until played).",
      'Follow suit; if unable, must play a trump. Highest trump or highest of led suit wins trick.',
      "Positive contracts: declarer's side needs 36+ of 70 card points. Negative: lose every trick, or take exactly one or two tricks, or fewest points.",
      'Bonuses (Trull, Pagat Ultimo, Valat, etc.) and kontra/rekontra double scores; announcements before play.',
    ],
