      'Setup example: 12 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: In positive contracts, the declarer's side must take at least 36 of the 70 available card points. Negative contracts have objectives like losing all tricks or winning an exact number of tricks.",
      "Turn-flow example: Deal 12 cards each and 6 to talon. Auction to determine declarer and contract. In king-calling contracts declarer names a suit; holder of that king is partner (hidden until king is played). Declarer may exchange with talon in some contracts. Announcements (bonuses, kontra) then play. Follow suit; must trump if unable. Highest trump or highest of led suit wins trick. Count card points; declarer's side needs 36+ in positive contracts.",
      "Scoring example: Standard KÃ¶nigrufen scoring applies with RuÃŸbach-specific values for contracts and bonuses. In positive contracts declarer's side wins by taking at least 36 of 70 card points (plus talon share). In negative contracts win by losing every trick (Bettel), taking exactly one or two tricks (Piccolo/Zwiccolo), or taking fewest points (Trischaken). Bonuses (Trull, Pagat Ultimo, Valat, etc.) score game points independently..",
